\par\par \b \uc2 Colombian cenbank faces struggle in curbing peso   \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2007\par 22:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, June 5 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will find it increasingly tough to curb the peso's appreciation with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  without threatening the inflation target for this year, a bank official said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Fernando Tenjo, one of the seven \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board members, noted the conflict between the bank snapping up dollars to slow the peso's surge against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while also attracting foreign capital by hiking interest rates to ease inflationary pressures.   \par \par \uc2 Short-term foreign capital is flowing into Colombia attracted by interest rates but at the same time pressuring the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has appreciated around 17 percent so far this year against the greenback.   \par \par \uc2 "To step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the same time we are bringing up the interest rates in Colombia along with the rest of the world could practically become suicide," Tenjo said at a conference. "This works against us and against Colombians."   \par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its key interest rate 2.75 percentage points since April last year to the current 8.75 percent. But Tenjo did not say whether the bank had considered abandoning its current policy of hiking rates.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also purchased around $4.9 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year directly or through auctions, but has failed to arrest a 19.25 percent climb in the peso <COP=RR> over the last 12 months.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Jose Dario Uribe recently told Congress that compared with Colombia's gross domestic product, the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases could be considered the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of any such institution in the world.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 12-month inflation had reached 6.23 percent by May, and analysts forecast that it will now be difficult for Colombia to reach its consumer price target for the year of between 3.5 percent and 4.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Most experts estimate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep hiking its interest rate to 9 percent or more.   \par \par \uc2 "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market only when we do not put in danger the inflation target and it is more difficult now to make these two objectives compatible and still combat inflationary pressures," Tenjo said.   \par \par \uc2 Colombia's economy is growing rapidly, driven by domestic demand and the flow of foreign investment. The gross domestic product expanded 6.8 percent last year, and the government expects growth of between 5 percent and 5.5 percent this year.   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-COLOMBIA/CENBANK|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070605e365001rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
