\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens A Bit As Treasury  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 ,Stocks Dn   \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2007\par 00:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, May 29, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso Tuesday weakened slightly as the Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to stop the rapid appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid an active session.   \par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso closed at COP1,917.00 to the U.S. dollar, but that was after it hit COP1,900.00 in midmorning from the COP1,916.25 closing mark Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Total trading volume reached $1.21 billion, the fourth highest volume so far this year. That compares with a daily average of $694 million in April.   \par \par \uc2 Investment bank Corficolombiana said in a report the peso appreciated earlier in the session tracking other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Mexican peso and the Brazilian real.   \par \par \uc2 "However, when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached COP1,900 the Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a maximum of COP1,933," Corficolombiana said.   \par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso has appreciated 16.8% so far this year even though the government last week announced capital controls on foreign portfolio investment and even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $4.52 billion in the spot market in the first four months of the year.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, Finance Minister Oscar Ivan Zuluaga said the government is open to introducing new measures in an effort to stop the strong appreciation of the peso.   \par \par \uc2 The government will also evaluate whether to extend a measure introduced Wednesday forcing foreign portfolio holders to deposit 40% of their investments in an account at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for six months without interest.   \par \par \uc2 The measure complements two measures announced more than three weeks ago designed to discourage capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 In the equity market, the Colombian benchmark stock index retreated 0.1% to 10,139.10 points, the fourth consecutive decline following the capital controls measure.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market increased at the opening of the session, but retreated, tracking the U.S. stock market's early decline Tuesday, Corficolombiana added.   \par \par \uc2 The sharpest drop came from textile company Fabricato (FABRICATO.OB), which retreated 2.5% to COP57.50. Fabricato was the most heavily traded stock with about a third of Tuesday's total trading volume ot COP64.20 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Preferred shares of the country's largest bank Bancolombia (BCOLOMBIA.BO) decreased 0.8% to COP13,500.   \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, the yield on the benchmark peso denominated TES maturing in 2020 fell 0.019 percentage point to 9.855%.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Diana Delgado, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-6001980; diana.delgado@dowjones.com\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 05-29-07 1835ET   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070529e35t003si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
