\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens Sharply On Ctrl Bk Measure, \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 23:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Mar 30, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a measure to stop the galloping peso. The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recorded its highest trading volume since 1997 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began tracking the data.   \par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso closed at 2,202.30 to the dollar, compared with COP2,147.80 on Thursday. Total trading volume jumped to $1.50 billion on Friday, compared with a daily volume of $903.7 million in February.   \par \par \uc2 The peso weakened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a measure under which it aims to reduce the amount of pesos in the financial system by offering to pay interest to commercial banks that hand over their excess cash.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market by buying dollars, said Cesar Tovar, an analyst at the local unit of Standford Group.   \par \par \uc2 "At the opening of the session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed a bid to buy $180 million," Tovar said. "Today, it showed that it has the intention not to let the peso appreciate further." .   \par \par \uc2 The peso has appreciated 3.8% so far this year despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  having bought $2.02 billion in the spot market in January and February.   \par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso appreciated 27% in the 2002-2006 period because of an inflow of dollars from foreign direct investment, remittances from Colombians living abroad and foreign portfolio investment.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Colombian benchmark stock index ended lower, dragged down again by steel maker  \uc2 Acerias Paz del Rio\uc2  (PAZRIO.BO), which slid 5.8% to COP81.50 after dropping 8% Thursday. The IGBC stock index fell 1.1% to 10,686.38.   \par \par \uc2 Paz del Rio was the most heavily traded stock, accounting for about half of Friday's total volume of COP46.91 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Shares of Paz del Rio fell after its new owner, Brazilian industrial  \uc2 group Votorantim\uc2 , said Friday it won't buy shares from minority shareholders after it secured a 52% stake in the Colombian steel maker.   \par \par \uc2 On March 16, Votorantim offered to pay in an auction COP131.42 for each Paz del Rio share, or COP1.078 trillion Colombian pesos ($489.4 million).   \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, the yield on the benchmark peso-denominated TES maturing in 2020 increased 0.077 percentage point to 9.839%.   \par \par \uc2 The yield increased as investors sold TES to purchase dollars, Tovar said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado, Dow Jones Newswires; 57-1-600-1980; diana.delgado@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 03-30-07 1737ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070330e33u003dt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
