\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Colombia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  moves to curb peso strength   \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 16:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts; adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, March 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso retreated nearly 2.5 percent on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought up to $1 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and announced other measures to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.   \par \par \uc2 The bank bought between $800 million and $1 billion on Friday, market sources said, prompting the Colombian peso <COP=RR> to slide 2.48 percent against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Until early on Friday, the peso had strengthened 5.75 percent over the last 12 months to 2,155 per greenback.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that starting on Monday it will allow banks to hold interest-bearing deposits for up to two weeks at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The move is intended to help mop up excess liquidity created by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ongoing dollar purchases, setting the stage for bigger \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Also on Friday, the bank sold put options to buy $161 million, a measure it takes regularly to control peso volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The stronger peso has sparked complaints from Colombian exporters who say their products have become less competitive overseas.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is doing everything it can think of to stop the peso from strengthening, but it may not succeed." said Alberto Ramos, senior economist at Goldman Sachs in New York.   \par \par \uc2 "The more it tries to control the peso the higher the probability that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will start to conflict with the achievement of the bank's own inflation targets," Ramos said.   \par \par \uc2 Buying dollars tends to increase the supply of pesos in the economy and push inflation higher.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started periodically raising rates almost a year ago to hit its inflation targets, set at 3.5 percent to 4.5 percent for 2007.   \par \par \uc2 In 2006, inflation totaled 4.48 percent but it has speeded up since then to 5.25 percent in the 12 months through February.   \par \par \uc2 The Andean country's overnight interest rate is now 8.25 percent and expected to climb.   \par \par \uc2 Gross domestic product grew by 6.8 percent last year in its healthiest expansion since 1978, driven by foreign investment, privatizations, high consumer borrowing, a construction boom and strong prices fetched by oil and coal exports.   \par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-OPTIONS/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070330e33u001kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
