\par\par \b \uc2 Colombian Peso Appreciates Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2007\par 21:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso strengthened Wednesday even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on the spot market in an effort to contain the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso closed at 2,216.50 to the dollar, compared with COP2,222.90 the previous day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached its highest level since Jan. 3. Trading volume in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was the highest so far this year at $1.25 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in the spot market after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaked at COP2,216.00 to the dollar at the end of the session, said Moira Harris, head of research at local brokerage Profesionales de Bolsa.  \par \par \uc2 The peso also came under pressure as foreign funds sold dollars, Harris said.  \par \par \uc2 Daniel Nino, managing director of research at the country's largest bank, Bancolombia, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought about $300 million in the past week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acquired $1 billion in the spot market in January.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Colombian benchmark stock index advanced after comments from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke, who said he is comfortable with current interest-rate levels. Bernanke also said factors contributing to inflationary risks appear to be waning.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark index IGBC advanced 0.8% to 10,896.37 points.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of the country's largest holding Suramericana de Inversiones (SURAMINV.BO) advanced 1% to COP20,160.  \par \par \uc2 Suramericana accounted for about one-third of Wednesday's total trading volume of COP115.78 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Holding Valores Simesa (VALSIMESA.BO) posted the sharpest rise in Wednesday's market. It rose 7.8% to COP1,800.  \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, the yield on the benchmark peso-denominated TES maturing in 2020 declined 0.128 percentage point to 9.326%.  \par \par \uc2 According to Nino, the yield fell after the government announced Tuesday it will use COP1.07 trillion in extra tax revenue to prepay foreign and local debt later this year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-6001980; diana.delgado@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-02-07 2055GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1845 5071  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070214e32e00106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
