\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Colombia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  hikes rate; economy strong  \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2007\par 19:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, analyst comments)  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Jan 26 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its key interest rate by a quarter percentage point to 7.75 percent to stem inflationary pressures as the economy shows strong growth, the government said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Alberto Carrasquilla, after a meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, told reporters that he expected economic growth for last year to be "well above" 6 percent. The Andean nation's economy grew more than 5 percent in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 It was the seventh time the bank has raised the rate since April last year and analysts expect at least one more rise of 25 basis points to bring the rate to the optimum level to control inflation without trimming economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board said a statement that it expects Colombia to met its 4.48 percent inflation target for 2006 and its target of 3.5 to 4.5 percent for this year.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to push rates higher; with the key monetary policy rate reaching at least 8 percent by June 2007," Goldman Sachs economist Alberto Ramos said in a research note to clients.  \par \par \uc2 Carrasquilla said the bank would keep making "substantial" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem local peso fluctuations.  \par \par \uc2 The minister said the government would counter those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure that \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  met its inflation targets. But he said the government did not intend to sell local peso-denominated TES bonds to counter those measures.  \par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-RATES/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070126e31q00233\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
