\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Colombia peso ends down 2.15 pct in regional selloff  \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2006\par 20:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Colombia, May 15 (Reuters) - Colombia's peso closed trading on Monday down 2.15 percent at 2,437.5 against the U.S. dollar in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharpest fall since December 2004 as emerging markets slumped on concerns over U.S. interest rates, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they expected \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by exercising a call option for the auction sale of $180 million to ease the peso's volatility on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "According to the norms of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is almost certain that tomorrow they will sell," said Carolina Parra an analyst with local Bancafe.  \par \par \uc2 The slide in the peso followed similar drops in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region as U.S. bond prices dipped and raw material prices fell. The peso's fall slowed toward the end of the session as traders expected pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease.  \par \par \uc2 "We saw calm returns ... as other markets calmed down and people regained their direction," said Arnoldo Casas, an analyst at the Bogota-based Promotora Bursatil.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -COLOMBIA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060515e25f002kj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
