\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Sept $710 Mln   \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2005\par 23:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $710 million in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in September, considered its second strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a press release Monday.   \par \par \uc2 That brought the total amount of dollar purchases by the bank in the first nine months of the year to a net $3.550 billion as it tried to stem the peso's appreciation against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso has strengthened 3.8% against the dollar so far this year, adding onto gains of more than 18% in 2004.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $2.4 billion on such \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Local analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could purchase an additional $2 billion between October and December, as the sharpest influx of dollars is arriving in the last quarter of the year.   \par \par \uc2 Coffee growers could repatriate at least $400 million of their profits between October and December, as the year's best coffee harvest in produced in the last quarter.   \par \par \uc2 South African SABMiller (SAB.JO) could bring at least $630 million in November, as it will make a cash offer of $19.48 per share to minority shareholders of recently acquired Grupo Empresarial Bavaria (BAVARIA.BO).   \par \par \uc2 Strong portfolio and foreign direct investment inflows, remittances from Colombians living overseas and trade-related flows should also boost the peso.   \par \par \uc2 The government has tried just about everything to stem the galloping peso. It imposed some capital controls on portfolio investments last December, but officials recently indicated they are likely to lift the restrictions in the coming months. It also shut its reverse repurchase window in December.   \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-600-1980; colombia@dowjones.com [ 10-10-05 2126GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051010e1aa000u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
