\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  to continue "aggressive"  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2005\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds research note, explanation)  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue "aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop the peso appreciating against the dollar and plans to help businesses hurt by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, Finance Minister Alberto Carrasquilla said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The government now expects the peso <COP=> to be stronger next year than it had originally thought and has altered its forecast for the average 2006 exchange rate to 2,400 per dollar from 2,498, the minister told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "We are going to continue supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. They have been particularly aggressive and will continue to be so. We support them, we back them and we are united with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on that issue," Carrasquilla said.  \par \par \uc2 Asked how long the authorities would continue buying dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Carrasquilla replied: "Until the limits of fiscal and monetary prudence, which are a long way off at the moment."  \par \par \uc2 Carrasquilla on Wednesday described the effect of the high peso, which makes it harder for Colombian exports to compete, as a "\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurricane". He said the government was preparing measures to assist businesses hurt by the strength of the peso, but gave no details.  \par \par \uc2 The peso has risen by almost 10 percent against the U.S. dollar over the past 12 months, due to factors including high interest rates offered by Colombian government bonds, foreign direct investment, a trade surplus and remittances from Colombians working abroad.  \par \par \uc2 The rise has come despite dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  totaling $5.75 billion since the beginning of 2004 and purchases by the government of at least an additional $700 million.  \par \par \uc2 The purchases have been accompanied by large government bond sales to make sure the excess pesos do not cause inflation, in a process known as "sterilization".  \par \par \uc2 But eventually continued dollar purchases could cause inflation, warned Alberto Ramos, a senior economist at Goldman Sachs in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "So far the heavy partially sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not conflicted with the inflation target due to the significant increase in the demand for pesos, by both residents and non-residents, at the positive impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation on tradable inflation. However, such a conflict is bound to arise at a later stage if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows of the magnitude we have seen recently continue," Ramos said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 The peso was slightly weaker on Thursday at 2,298 per dollar, after closing at 2,292 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 This minor depreciation was caused partly by suspicions the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could announce interest rate cuts at its board meeting on Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050915e19f001pq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppic