\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Colombia's Peso Weakens; Stocks, Bonds Gain Ground  \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Apr 04, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened slightly as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again Monday while the local stock exchange ended higher, powered by shares from Corfivalle and Bavaria.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at COP2,377.50 to the dollar compared with COP2,373.50 on Friday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading volume totaled $428.18 million.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be buying dollars in the spot market, part of an ongoing strategy to cap the peso's appreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the benchmark IGBC stock index rose 0.8% to close at 4,720.81 points.  \par \par \uc2 The largest advance came from preferential shares of financial institution Corfivalle, which jumped 10% to close at COP5,400.00.  \par \par \uc2 The most heavily traded stock was Bavaria (BAVARIA.BO), South America's second-largest brewer, which rose 7.9% to close at COP41,000.00.  \par \par \uc2 In the local debt market, the yield on the benchmark 2012 TES Treasury note ended at 12.32%, 0.01 percentage point lower than Friday's closing mark.  \par \par \uc2 The debt market was influenced by news late Friday that Colombian consumer prices dropped 0.77% in March from the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 The debt market was also positively affected by the announcement that the Colombian government prepaid a $1.25 billion loan from the Inter-American Development Bank on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-600-1980; colombia@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 04-04-05 1810ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050404e144006w9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
