\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia's Peso Gains To Ctrl Bank's Chagrin; TES Yld Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2005\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso strengthened again Tuesday despite apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and local debt also gained ground. But stocks fell a hair thanks a decline in market heavyweight Bancolombia.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended at at COP2,322, versus COP2,333 in the previous session, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volume climbing to $453 million from $400 million Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The peso's advance could have been greater were it not for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dealers reported was present in the market, said Marco Castrillon, an analyst a Bogota-based brokerage Afin.  \par \par \uc2 Jose Dario Uribe, Colombia's new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, took over Tuesday, vowing to keep interest rates low to fuel economic growth and to stem the strong appreciation of the peso. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added, would also continue in an effort to curb the peso's rise.  \par \par \uc2 But Castrillion said the comments had little effect because Uribe, who's not related to President Alvaro Uribe, had already relayed the same message in recently.  \par \par \uc2 The peso appreciated 18.2% against the dollar last year, despite nearly $4 billion in estimated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government agencies. Exporters complained bitterly that their competitiveness was being undermined by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strengthening, and President Uribe also called for more action.  \par \par \uc2 Apart from the dollar's global weakness, strong portfolio and direct investment inflows, alongside Colombian worker remittances from abroad and trade-related inflows, have all bolstered the peso, and analysts say the trend isn't like to change anytime soon.  \par \par \uc2 In the local debt market, the yield on the 2012 TES continued to drop thanks to bullish inflation and improving debt data. Colombia's consumer price index rose 0.3% in December from the previous month, matching analysts' forecasts and bringing the full-year 2004 CPI to 5.5%, which hit the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 5.5%-to-6% targeted range.  \par \par \uc2 The 2004 inflation reading was the lowest in half a century. Uribe also pledged to guide inflation down to 5% this year.  \par \par \uc2 The stock of Colombia's total external debt, meanwhile, amounted to $38.55 billion in September, or 41% of gross domestic product, up from $37.73 billion, or 48% of GDP, the year before. The decline in the ratio is a result of the peso's appreciation and an expanding economy.  \par \par \uc2 In the stock market, the common shares of financial Bancolombia (CIB) fell 0.1% to COP7,990, likely dragged lower by a 3.3% fall to $13.58 in the country's American Depositary Receipt. ADRs from emerging markets were broadly lower on a surge in the U.S. dollar, which was drawing investors away from emerging market equities, New York-based traders said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Charles Roth, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2226; charles.roth@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-01-05 2101GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1068 1845  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050104e114000mw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
