\par\par \b \uc2 New  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk Head:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Continue  \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2005\par 17:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief has vowed to keep interest rates low to fuel economic growth and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue adjusting rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the appreciation of the peso, local broadcaster Caracol reported.  \par \par \uc2 Jose Dario Uribe, who took over the post Tuesday from Miguel Urrutia Montoya, couldn't be reached for comment, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's press department confirmed the statements.  \par \par \uc2 "The two instruments will continue to be used to the maximum to try to - with low interest rates and the accumulation of (international) reserves - have a positive effect on the exchange rate," Caracol quoted Uribe saying.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ($1=COP2,333) appreciated 18.2% against the dollar last year, despite nearly $4 billion in estimated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government agencies. Exporters complained bitterly that their competitiveness was being undermined by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strengthening, and President Alvaro Uribe - no relation to the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief - also called for more action.  \par \par \uc2 The new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will aim to slow the growth of inflation to 5% this year, after it moderated to 5.5% in 2004, its slowest pace in half a century. At the same time, though, it will seek to promote economic growth, he said, according to Caracol.  \par \par \uc2 "To that end, interest rates will stay low and that...will continue until the economy receives the stimulus of monetary policy (sufficient) to grow and generate jobs," Uribe said.  \par \par \uc2 Colombia's economy grew close to an estimated 4% last year, after expanding 3.7% in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Uribe was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's technical director before taking over the top job.  \par \par \uc2 Web site:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.caracol.com.co"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.caracol.com.co }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Charles Roth, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2226; charles.roth@dowjones.com [ 04-01-05 1638GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050104e114000j2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
