\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Colombia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  cuts rates by 25 bps.   \b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2004\par 20:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Colombia, Dec 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday cut its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by 25 basis points and heeded a call from President Alvaro Uribe who expressed hope lower rates would stem a rise in the peso.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts had not expected the bank to follow Uribe's advice, although the bank said it was justified by low inflationary pressures. The president has said he fears a stronger peso will reduce Colombia's export earnings.   \par \par \uc2 "The decision was taken after analyzing medium-and long-term inflation projections," the bank said in a news release to announce the cuts after a board meeting.   \par \par \uc2 Colombian consumer prices rose by 5.82 percent in the 12 months to the end of November, putting the country on course to meet its 2004 inflation target of 5.0-6.0 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The bank's general manager Miguel Urrutia added at a news conference: "We take what has happened recently with the exchange rate into account when we analyze future inflation."   \par \par \uc2 The bank cut its minimum repurchase agreement rate to 6.5 percent. The repo rate is the one at which the bank lends short term to commercial banks.   \par \par \uc2 The minimum repo rate is only available in quotas. The bank also cut its "lombard" repo rate, for which loans have no fixed limit, to 10.25 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The bank cut its minimum reverse repo rate to 5.5 percent and its lombard reverse repo rate to 4.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Lower interest rates should weaken the peso by reducing returns for foreigners investing in Colombian assets, such as TES treasury bonds.   \par \par \uc2 But relatively high interest rates attracting dollars to Colombia are only part of the reason for the strength of the peso, which has risen by more than 15 percent over the past 12 months.   \par \par \uc2 The peso has also been bolstered by improving security after 40 years of guerrilla war, and by rising exports and remittances from Colombian workers abroad.   \par \par \uc2 The rate cut came three days after Uribe announced restrictions on short-term foreign investment in treasury bonds and stocks, another measure meant to restrain the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The bank's first rate reduction since March, when it also made a 25-basis-point cut, did not phase the peso , which closed 10.5 pesos higher per greenback at 2,353 on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The bank also said it would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in 2005. So far this year, it has together with the government bought about $3 billion in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to hold back the peso.   \par \par \uc2 The bank also said it would complete this year its planned sale of $180 million in foreign reserves to the government, which wants to use them to pay off foreign debt.   \par \par \uc2 It has also agreed with the government to study the possibility of more such sales in 2005. The bank's reserves currently stand at more than $13 billion.   \par \par \uc2 As of next year, the bank said it will begin to pay interest to local financial institutions which deposit pesos in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vaults. The measure is aimed at reducing the inflationary impact of dollar purchases.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041217e0ch00gcy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
