\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Weaker On Ctrk Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stks Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 21:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened modestly Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased U.S. dollars in the spot market. The stock market, meanwhile, finished higher for the second consecutive session.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at COP2,480.70 to the dollar compared to COP2,476.90 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently said it intends to purchase $1 billion in the spot market to contain the peso appreciation. But analysts have begun questioning the effectiveness of the measure, given the peso's continued strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 "We heard the bank has purchased over $600 million of the total $1 billion. That explains why it has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively" of late, said Cesar Tovar, head of research at trading house Bolsa y Banca.  \par \par \uc2 The peso's performance is in line with that of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. The euro has been at all-time highs against the dollar for the past week. The euro retreated slightly to $1.3256 Monday from $1.3294 in New York late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Meantime, the benchmark IGBC stocks index finished up 1.3% at 4,253.22 points. Trading volume stood at COP15.90 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Holding Valores Bavaria (VALBAVARIA.BO) led the advancers, finishing up 6.4% at COP468.00, while the preferential shares of Corfivalle (CORFIVALLE.BO) rose 3.9% to COP2,595.00.  \par \par \uc2 Valores Bavaria's chief will host a press conference late today where he is expected to announce administrative changes at the organization.  \par \par \uc2 On the debt market, yields on the benchmark TES finished at 12.72%, 0.10 percentage point higher from Friday's closing. Total trading volume reached more than COP2.896 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-600-1980; colombia@dowjones.com [ 29-11-04 2018GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1068 1845  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041129e0bt000y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
