\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens Amid Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stks Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2004\par 23:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened sharply Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market by purchasing dollars, traders said, while stocks continued to rally amid strong trading volume.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at COP2,581.70 to the dollar compared to COP2,561.00 on Wednesday. Trading volume was hefty at $746.9 million.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market experienced strong volatility. The peso will keep weakening if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market," said Alvaro Camaro, head of research at brokerage Promotora Bursatil. "However, in the coming days, coffee growers and (state oil company) Ecopetrol could monetize some dollars as a result of their exports,"  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced last week that it plans to purchase $1 billion through the end of the year, via its first spot market dollar purchase since 1999 and through put options. Colombian authorities have been moving aggressively to stem the appreciation of the peso to ensure that Colombian exports maintain their price competitiveness on international markets.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, yields on the benchmark TES maturing in 2012 finished at 13.41%, 0.05 percentage point higher than Wednesday's closing mark. Total TES volume reached COP2.08 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 On the equities market, the benchmark IGBC index finished up 1.91% at 3,695.99 points. Trading volume was at its highest level in a week, at COP30.59 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The sharpest advancers were shares of Suramericana de Inversiones (SURAMINV.BO) and Corfinsura (CORFINSURA.BO), amid ongoing merger talk. Colombia's largest bank, Bancolombia (CIB), said a week ago it is poised to merge with Corfinsura and mortgage bank Conavi.  \par \par \uc2 Corfinsura gained 9.5% to finish at COP7,450.00, while Suramericana de Inversiones ended up 7% at COP7,370.00  \par \par \uc2 Colombian stocks have advanced 58% so far this year amid optimism about the country's economy, which has boosted consumer and investor sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado; Dow Jones Newswires; 571-600-1980; colombia@dowjones.com [ 23-09-04 2130GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1068 1845  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040923e09n000xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
