\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Weakens As Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  On Spot Mkt   \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2004\par 23:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market by purchasing dollars, traders said, while yields on TES Treasury notes rose in reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements.   \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at COP2,569.50 to the dollar compared to COP2,542.50 on Monday. Trading volume was hefty at $676.25 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Friday that it plans to purchase $1 billion through the end of the year, via its first spot market dollar purchase since 1999 and through put options.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't know how much it bought, but it seems to be a strong amount based on the market reaction," said Carlos Silva, analyst at local brokerage Ultrabursatiles.   \par \par \uc2 Colombian authorities have been moving aggressively to stem the appreciation of the peso to ensure that Colombian exports maintain their price competitiveness on international markets.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closed 15 minutes before the U.S. Federal Reserve confirmed market expectations by announcing a 25 basis-point increase in its key federal fund rates, to 1.75%.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, as part of a strategy to sell $138 million worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to the government, state-run Banco de la Republica purchased COP350 billion of TES from the markets. On Wednesday, the government's Public Credit department will add COP350 billion to its regular weekly TES auction, so as not to create distortions in the monetary base.   \par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark TES maturing in 2012 finished at 13.42%, 0.19 percentage point higher than Monday's closing mark. Total TES volume reached COP2 trillion.   \par \par \uc2 On the equities market, the benchmark IGBC index finished up 0.32% at 3,598.40 points. A total of COP22.30 billion in shares traded hands.   \par \par \uc2 For the second consecutive day, the sharpest advancers were shares in the two largest textile companies in the country. Coltejer (COLTEJER.BO) gained 22% to close at COP21.90, while Fabricato-Tejicondor (FABRICATO.BO) rose 17.5% to COP22.20. Trading in both stocks was halted during the middle of the session as local bourse regulations require that trading stop on stocks that advance more than 10%.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors are taking advantage of those stocks not only because they remain cheap, but also because both companies have tremendous opportunities to keep advancing," said Edgar Jimenez, equities analyst at Promotora Bustatil.   \par \par \uc2 Colombian stocks have posted significant gains this year amid optimism about the country's economy, which has boosted consumer and investor sentiment.   \par \par \uc2 -By Diana Delgado; Dow Jones Newswires; 571-600-1980; colombia@dowjones.com [ 21-09-04 2155GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1068 1845   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040921e09l000x3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
