it has bought over the past month to $480 million.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts say monetary authorities must beware of pumping too many pesos into the market without fueling inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Colombia has a 2004 inflation target of a maximum 5-6 percent, compared to 6.49 percent in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 The peso gained 2.1 percent against the dollar in 2003, a year in which the government initially forecast depreciation of 6-8 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040115e01f003nj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
