\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia TES Note Yields Fall As Lower Inflation Expected  \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2004\par 21:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--Yields fell across the board Wednesday at the Colombian government's weekly auction of peso-denominated TES treasury notes amid continued peso strength and expectations of lower January inflation, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry said in a statement that the yield on two-year notes fell 15 basis points from the last sale Dec. 10, while the four-year note dipped 20 basis points. The five-year note fell 50 basis points, while the 10-year note shed 25 basis points, also from the Dec. 10 sale.  \par \par \uc2 One-year notes were not sold Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 In explaining the lower yields, Ricardo Duran, an analyst at local brokerage Corredores Asociados, pointed to preliminary private estimates for Colombia's January inflation that say consumer prices rose by a lesser percentage than they did in that month of 2003, when inflation was 1.17%.  \par \par \uc2 Also, Duran said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures announced by \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday have so far done little to stem further peso strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry said it sold 300 billion pesos ($1=COP2,746.50) of TES's at the following terms Wednesday:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Maturity      Yld      Coupon    Amount     Demand \par             (annual)  (annual)  (COP Bln)  (COP Bln) \par May  27/05   9.79%      10%       29         229 \par Nov  9/07    12.44%     12%      103         310 \par Aug 22/08    12.49%     15%       81         281 \par Apr 26/12    13.54%     15%       87         289   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All notes are due for settlement Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-600-1980; colombia@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040114e01e000sy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
