\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's Cenbank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2003\par 19:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to bolster the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by auctioning up to $1 billion from its foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  It set the sale of first auction of dollar options for Feb. 27 at $200 million. \par \par \uc2  The peso, which lost 25 percent of its value against the dollar in 2002, has depreciated 4 percent against the greenback so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Colombia has agreed with the International Monetary Fund to a 2003 inflation target of 5.5 percent, which analysts warn could be jeopardized by the peso's recent tumble. Inflation in January alone reached a higher-than-expected 1.17 percent. \par \par \uc2  Latin America's fifth-largest economy had foreign reserves of $10.6 billion as of Feb. 5. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030214dz2e00zt7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
