\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Weaker Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Dn \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2002\par 21:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA -(Dow Jones)- The Colombian peso closed weaker against the dollar Wednesday, shrugging off a sale of call options by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was designed to boost the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The closing exchange rate rose to COP2887.00 to the dollar from Tuesday's close of COP2885.00, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The day's trading range was COP2856.00 to COP2892 to the dollar, on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume of $305.5 million. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's anti-volatility control measures, financial institutions still need dollars to lengthen their short positions and non-financial corporations are asking for U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , too," said Juan Pablo Barney, a trader at local bank Banco de Credito. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Wednesday sold call options through which it can sell up to $180 million to the market. \par \par \uc2  Demand was $599 million. The bank will announce later Wednesday how many options were exercised in the day's session. \par \par \uc2  The bank is required to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the benchmark Representative Market Rate, or TRM, is more than 4.0% above or below the 20-day moving average. Wednesday's TRM slightly surpassed this level, triggering the action. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's weighted average - the basis for Thursday's benchmark Representative Market Rate or TRM - was COP2888.32. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman said she didn't know what the trigger level for Thursday is, but said it's possible the bank will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  The Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped 21% against the dollar for the year to date against inflation of 4.92% through August. \par \par \uc2  On the equities side, share prices on the Colombian Stock Exchange closed lower Wednesday as Valores Bavaria reversed course to end sharply down. \par \par \uc2  The IGBC general index fell 0.80% to 1255.91 points, from 1266.11 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Total trading volume was COP2.035 billion. \par \par \uc2  Valores Bavaria, which had risen 65% in the past five sessions, fell 16% Wednesday to COP152. \par \par \uc2  Regulators asked Valores Bavaria on Tuesday to explain its earlier rises, but the company has so far not responded publicly. \par \par \uc2  The leading gainer was beer maker Bavaria, sister company to Valores Bavaria. It rose 0.2% to COP8855. \par \par \uc2  The IGBC index has gained 17.3% this year. It rose 2.6% in the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-602-1203; colombia@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1068 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021002dya20013k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
