\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia Ctrl Bk Keeps Inflation Goal Despite Peso Slide \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2002\par 00:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA -(Dow Jones)- Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't think a recent slide by the country's peso ($1=COP2664) endangers the official 6.0% inflation projection for 2002, bank governor Miguel Urrutia told a news conference Friday. \par \par \uc2  Urrutia told Dow Jones Newswires after the press conference that year-to-date depreciation is close to 15%. \par \par \uc2  "We believe 15% isn't enough to have effects for the inflation target," he said. "It's manageable, although what we don't know is how much the year's depreciation will end up at." \par \par \uc2  He added that an exchange rate at around the current level is probably good for the economy, as it helps exporters without putting too much pressure on local prices. \par \par \uc2  But he added that sharp movements and volatility in the exchange rate are not desirable, "and that's why we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  sometimes," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week sold $266 million to the market, through the exercise of dollar call options, to support the sagging peso. \par \par \uc2  The peso has floated freely since 1999, but anti-volatility rules - triggered for the first time Monday - require the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling call options whenever a day's average exchange rate is 4.0% above the 20-day moving average. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  erosion on inflation is muted by the relatively low weighting imports have in the basket of goods and services used for Colombia's consumer price index. \par \par \uc2  Most food - the heaviest weighted group, with 30% of the total - is produced locally. And while international oil prices influence gasoline costs, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth these locally. \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires survey of seven analysts Friday produced an average inflation projection of 6.05% for 2002 as a whole. \par \par \uc2  -By Mary Morrison, Dow Jones Newswires; 571-602-1402; colombia@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020802dy820019r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
