\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 3-Colombia Cenbank cuts rates by 50 basis points. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Stewart \par \uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2001\par 23:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates with market closing, Cenbank statement, paras 7-9,12,13) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Colombia, Nov 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday cut its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by 50 basis points, slightly above market expectations, the bank's sixth rate reduction this year. \par \par \uc2  With the cut, Colombia's one-day reverse repurchase agreement rate stands at 7.75 percent, and repos are at 8.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  Of 27 analysts surveyed on Thursday by Reuters, 17 had forecast a rate cut of 25 basis points and six forecast a 50 basis point reduction. \par \par \uc2  Economists cheered the bank's decision, saying the move was justified by a declining inflation rate, a still sluggish Colombian economy and rate cuts this week by the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I was expecting 25 (basis points), so this was a good surprise," said Alberto Bernal, a Colombia analyst at IDEA Global in New York. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing significant coordination between world central banks ... I personally think there is room for further cuts if world interest rates continue doing what they're doing," he added. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's stock index rallied on the news to close 1.53 percent higher, as investors saw cheaper credit for indebted companies and likely more available cash to invest in shares. \par \par \uc2  "Since the drop was larger than expected, some investors may begin to seek higher yields and eventually that will be in the stock market," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended virtually unchanged at 2,302 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  INFLATION TAME \par \par \uc2  Colombia, Latin America's fifth largest economy, is widely expected to meet an 8 percent ceiling for consumer inflation in 2001 as agreed with the IMF. Last week, it reported inflation of 0.19 percent in October, bringing consumer price increases to 7.16 percent for the first 10 months of the year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have fallen by 325 basis points since the beginning of the year. The bank last cut rates by a lower-than-expected 25 basis points on Oct. 12. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement the rate cut would not jeopardize its targets and forecast declining rates of inflation next year. \par \par \uc2  "Medium-term projections for inflation forecast a decline in this variable, consistent with achieving the 6 percent inflation target for the end of 2002," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  Although economists said that the rate reductions could put pressure on Colombia's ambitious 2002 inflation target, they said the cuts were crucial to reactivate the economy. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's $87 billion economy has been hit this year by Marxist-rebel bombings of key oil infrastructure, plunging coffee prices and a world economic slowdown which has weakened the market for the war-torn Andean nation's exports. \par \par \uc2  The country's 37-year-old guerrilla war has claimed 40,000 lives in the past decade alone, and the government has said the conflict annually shaves off about 25 percent from gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  The government currently forecasts 2001 growth at between 2.2 percent and 2.4 percent, down from from 3.8 percent originally. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's peso has depreciated by 3.38 percent since the beginning of the year, far less than in other South American nations, including Brazil where the real has weakened by almost 23 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011109dxb900u5f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
