\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Colombia cuts rates 100 bps, shrugs off Argentina. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Stewart \par \uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2001\par 19:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates throughout with analyst quotes, bank statement, background, market reaction) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Colombia, Aug 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates on Thursday by a higher-than-expected 100 basis points, citing a June economic slowdown and relative isolation from Argentina's debt default fears. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that Colombia's peso was "relatively stable" even as fallout from Argentina punished \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil and Chile, and added the rate cut would not affect 2001 and 2002 inflation targets. \par \par \uc2  The move surprised economists, who had forecast a much more conservative rate cut of between 20 and 50 basis points. Economists cheered the decision, however, saying it was sound and would help jump-start Latin America's fifth largest economy. \par \par \uc2  "Having really no direct links to Argentina, the economy is trading more in tune with the global economy. There's a slowdown, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is cutting rates," said Siobhan Manning, emerging market strategist at Italian investment bank Caboto. \par \par \uc2  Colombia peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on the news, rising to 2,285 per dollar, up from Thursday's open of 2,290. On the J.P. Morgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus (EMBI+), Colombia's portion of the index widened 4 basis points over safe-haven U.S. Treasuries. \par \par \uc2  Despite a 37-year guerrilla war, Colombia has long enjoyed relative isolation in the face of debt woes ravaging neighboring economies. It has never defaulted on its debt, unlike Latin America's three biggest economies of Brazil, Mexico and Argentina. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Colombia has been the second best emerging market performer on the EMBI+ this year, ranking only behind Russia. \par \par \uc2  It raised $325 million on Tuesday by reopening its 2020 global bond, tapping demand from regional investors who were seeking to diversify their exposure away from cash-strapped Argentina - the region's No. 3 economy and its biggest foreign borrower. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only weakened 2.79 percent this year, well below inflation of 6.29 percent and a depreciation of 14 percent by the same time last year. \par \par \uc2  "Uncertainty generated by the situation in Argentina has not had large influence over the Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, judging by the relative stability of the exchange rate," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  But the economy has been hit by the world economic slowdown. The the government slashed it growth forecasts for 2001 and 2002 in late July, pegging growth at this year at 2.4 percent - down from it previous estimate of 3.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  The government revised its 2002 growth forecast to 4.0 percent from 4.0 percent previously. \par \par \uc2  "New indicators like industrial production show a deterioration in productive activity in June. Additionally, demand for money has been below reference lines, and there is room to increase (the supply)," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  With Thursday's rate cut, the third of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by 200 basis points in 2001. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010816dx8g00uet\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
