\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia's cenbank to boost foreign reserves. \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1999\par 22:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Nov 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced plans Friday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  sporadically in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to boost its net foreign reserves and smooth out any abrupt changes in the peso/dollar exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  The bank's net foreign reserves stood at just under $8 billion as of Nov. 10, the last date for which official figures are available, compared to more than $9 billion in March. \par \par \uc2  Rebuilding the reserve position was one of the commitments Colombia made under a recent loan agreement with the International Monetary Fund, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  To accumulate reserves, it said it would auction off special drawing rights, under which banks and other financial intermediaries would be entitled to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  $200 million in December and a total of $960 million next year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would only buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a month after each auction, however, and at an exchange rate below the market average over the previous 20 trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  Additionally, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would hold special auctions giving market players the option to sell or buy dollars from its coffers, whenever the peso traded 5 percent above or below its average trading level against the dollar over the previous 20 trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eliminated its closely managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime on Sept. 25, allowing the peso to float freely against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But Friday's measures will give it more leeway - aside from undeclared \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  through its financial intermediaries - to limit any exchange rate volatility going forward. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at 1,928 to the dollar Friday, well up from its low of 2,017 on Sept. 27. That was the first day of trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped the trading band under which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had moved against set limits against the dollar since 1994. \par \par \uc2  (( - Bogota newsroom, 571 523 7877, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbj09ogd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
