\par\par \b \uc2  Colombian Peso Ends Weaker After Chile Floats  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1999\par 21:15\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The Colombian peso weakened 0.3% Friday against the dollar, but fears of heavy speculation and a major drop following Chile's decision to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float were not realized, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The closing exchange rate rose to 1944.50 to the dollar from 1939.00 to the dollar Thursday. Friday's trading fluctuated between 1939.20 and its opening value of 1950.00 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $57.20 million. \par \par \uc2  "The peso started at its lowest point (against the dollar) on the day on expectations of speculation following Chile's decision to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float," a trader said. "But when speculation was limited, the peso recuperated ground over the day." \par \par \uc2  Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced late Thursday that it would suspend its formal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as one of the few countries that maintains a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band. \par \par \uc2  The peso moved Friday in the weaker half of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pre-set exchange rate band, which fixed a range of between COP1622.93 and COP1983.58 to the dollar for the day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fallen 20% against the greenback in the\par year to date. Since the trading band was weakened and widened in an\par effective devaluation June 27, the peso has depreciated by 10.6%.\par -By David Koop; 571-215-7132; dkoop@apbogota.org.co\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  03-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1915GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010827dv93004hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
