\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso -2: Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2 , Traders Say \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1999\par 21:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The Colombian peso (COP) ended 3.9% weaker Monday from its Friday close after being pushed off the weaker limit of its fixed trading band against the dollar by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The peso's closing exchange rate rose to COP1925.00 to the dollar from COP1850.00 to the dollar Friday. Monday's trading fluctuated between the opening level of COP1850.00 and the band ceiling of COP1956.32 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was $98.1 million. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold up to an estimated $45 million in the market, but no official comment was available. \par \par \uc2  A trader said the peso's recent slide - it had fallen 6.1% to Friday since a June 27 de facto devaluation - had gathered momentum as non-financial companies hurried to buy dollars in fear of further depreciation, and speculators joined in. \par \par \uc2  "There's strong demand from financial and non-financial companies which pushed up the dollar to the ceiling....And then there was a panic because there were problems in the trading system so people couldn't see what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was doing," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  "Underneath it all there's worry about the situation of the country, in particular now after all the violence over the weekend," another trader added. \par \par \uc2  A serious of bloody confrontations between leftist guerrillas and state forces have dominated Colombian news over the last couple of days. \par \par \uc2  A trader said that signs of a commitment to supporting the peso from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and public sector institutions - state oil company Ecopetrol (E.ECO) was also seen selling dollars - went some way towards calming market participants. \par \par \uc2  "But people get worried whenever the dollar's at the ceiling - and there's some concern about what will happen to the band," she added. \par \par \uc2  For Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pre-set exchange rate band fixed a range of between COP1600.62 and COP1956.32 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fallen 20% against the greenback in the\par year to date. Since the band was weakened and widened June 27, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has depreciated by 9.7%.\par -By Mary Morrison; 571-215-7132; mmorrison@apbogota.org.co\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-07-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1911GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7c057ze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
