\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  peso extends losses, despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1999\par 20:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, June 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso continued its downward slide Friday, as the market shrugged off massive efforts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  support. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported, moments after the market closed, that it sold $174.4 million from its reserves in a bid to lift the peso off the lower or weak end of its daily floating rate exchange band. But the embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which opened at the "floor" of the band, remained stuck there all day and closed at a new all-time low of 1,737.72. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was believed to be its biggest ever. And it followed the bank's sale of $110.4 million from its reserves Thursday, in the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since September of last year. \par \par \uc2  But the thinly-traded market, which handled just 93 transactions for a total of $193.6 million - including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales - failed to react to the seemingly futile effort to defend the peso from speculative attacks by banks and other financial intermediaries. \par \par \uc2  At least two transactions were carried out below the weak end of the trading band, including one shortly before the close in which someone purchased about $3 million at an exchange rate of 1,741.50 pesos to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Demand (for dollars) was even more intense than yesterday," said one trader, who added that the market was clearly betting on an imminent change in Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and a possible elimination of its crawling peg \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2  The peso lost just 58 centavos on the day but it slumped by more than 2.7 percent against the dollar this week and by more than 13.1 percent so far this year. \par \par \uc2  (( - Nelson Bocanegra, Bogota newsroom, 571 523 7877, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6p05kos\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
