\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  peso ends at new low despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1999\par 21:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOGOTA, June 24 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso\tab   ended at an all-time low against the dollar Thursday despite heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at propping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it sold $110.4 million from its reserves in a bid to lift the peso off the weak end of its daily floating rate exchange band, which was set for the day at 1,737.14.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  But the peso, which slumped to the 1,737.14 level in midday trade after testing a session high of 1,730, stayed stuck there throughout the rest of the trading session amid strong demand for dollars from banks and the corporate sector, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales, as it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, were the largest since Sept. 1 of last year, a day before the bank was forced to modify the exchange band in a de facto devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported 106 transactions in Thursday's trade for a total of $141.6 million, including the $110.4 million from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Juan Camilo Restrepo said earlier this week that he favoured a weaker peso as a way of fuelling export-led growth. Dealers said his comments contributed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 8.14 peso drop against the dollar Thursday, a nominal devaluation of 0.47 percent. \par \par \uc2  The peso, which has come under pressure as foreign investors ship capital out of recession-bound Colombia, has depreciated by 13.02 percent so far this year. \par \par \uc2  (( - Bogota newsroom, 571 523 7877, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6o05v8n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
