\par\par \b \uc2  Colombia cenbank says will limit  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  volatility. \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1999\par 19:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, April 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday that it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as often as necessary to limit volatility in trading of the country's peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In a statement issued after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's regular weekly policy meeting, its seven-member board said the peso would continue trading within the parameters of the exchange rate band set for it in September of last year, effectively ruling out any change in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  The peso fell to a three-month low Thursday, on recent statements by government officials, including President Andres Pastrana, who said its recent appreciation against the dollar was "unacceptable" because it was hurting the beleaguered export sector. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was widely reported to have sold dollars Thursday to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, said its board members had reiterated their "confidence" in the peso's current trading band and would keep the peso firmly within its limits. \par \par \uc2  "As it has done for several years, the Bank of the Republic (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the band, buying or selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to avoid extreme volatility in the exchange rate," the bank statement said. \par \par \uc2  The peso, which slumped to a record low of 1,605 against the dollar in early trading Friday, had firmed in late trade to 1,580, up eight pesos from Thursday's close at 1,586. \par \par \uc2  (( - Bogota newsroom, 571 523 7877, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv49037no\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
