\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  -2: Aim Of Mid-Exchange Band \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1999\par 00:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Juan Camilo Restrepo said Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act to weaken the peso, which has been strengthening against the dollar over recent weeks, with the aim of promoting economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Within the exchange rate band it seems much more desirable, much more beneficial to reactivate the economy, employment and exporting companies, that the exchange rate quotation be more at around the midpoint or the upper portion of the exchange rate band than at the floor... measures of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to that effect will be taken," Restrepo told journalists while leaving a congressional debate. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the midpoint of the preset exchange rate band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was COP1581.65 to the dollar. Pushing the peso down to that level would imply a 1.6% depreciation from Wednesday's closing exchange rate of COP1556.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso weakened Wednesday from Tuesday's close of COP1537.00 to the dollar, which traders said was in reaction to pro-depreciation comments made by President Andres Pastrana at a Tuesday night business forum in Medellin. \par \par \uc2  "The government is doing its part to impede... this absurd revaluationist tendency. May it be clear: the government considers it unacceptable that the exchange rate keeps falling as has happened in the last weeks," Pastrana said. \par \par \uc2  Restrepo said the exchange-rate band system worked well and would stay in place for the duration of the year. \par \par \uc2  Traders have noted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying on numerous occasions in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  -By Mary Morrison; 571-215-7132; mmorrison@apbogota.org.co \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-04-99 \par \par \uc2  2258GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4702mih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
