\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Shakes/Colombia -2: Hard To Cut Lending Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 1999\par 21:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "If the exchange rate only moved about a peso on a volatile day like Friday, this means there is confidence in Colombia's monetary policy makers," Villegas said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, but couldn't confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or quantify the amount. \par \par \uc2  As for the equity market, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  again weathered the storm better than some of its Latin American counterparts. The main IBB stock index slipped more than 6% in two days last week, as the world weighed the news that Brazil was widening the real's trading band, effectively devaluing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But on Friday, when Brazil announced its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the real, the IBB reversed its downtrend to post moderate gains. \par \par \uc2  At Tuesday's close, the IBB came in at 991.39, far below pre-float levels of around 1060, but without the wild swings seen in Argentina and Mexico. \par \par \uc2  Analysts attributed Colombia's muted reaction to external events to a lack of speculative foreign capital here and to positive sentiment generated by several fiscal policy initiatives introduced or overseen by Pastrana in the five months since he took office. Most notably, Pastrana decreed a 0.2% transactions tax in November aimed at bolstering a banking bailout fund, and pushed through Congress tax reforms aimed at increasing government revenues and narrowing a 4% fiscal deficit. \par \par \uc2  According to Villegas, such measures have set Colombia apart from other countries in the region, making it less likely that investors will group all Latin American nations together under the same high-risk banner during a crisis like this one. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-01-99 \par \par \uc2  2040GMT \par \par \uc2  1145 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1j00g89\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
