\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia central bank \highlight\uc2  details  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 1998\par 22:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Oct 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $4.5 million on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday in a bid to lend much-needed support to the peso. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which has remained under pressure ever since its de facto devaluation last month - tumbled 11.73 pesos against the dollar Monday to close at a new record low of 1,591.23. \par \par \uc2  The session marked the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to the lower limit of its exchange rate band since the band was raised by 9 percentage points on September 2. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold the $4.5 million from its reserves when the peso dropped to an intraday low of 1,591.24, the lower end of its exchange rate or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  But traders on the interbank or \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was actually seen selling dollars all day, through financial intermediaries. \par \par \uc2  The $4.5 million was just the small part of the bank's dollar sales that it did in its own name, the traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to draw heavily on its reserves before September 2, in an unsuccessful bid to defend the peso's earlier trading band. \par \par \uc2  It has vowed to maintain the new band until September of next year. But the bank's dwindling foreign reserves have dropped by more than $1.2 billion so far this year, and various financial analysts say another adjustment of the trading band may be necessary soon. \par \par \uc2  ((Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua5019y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
