\par\par \b \uc2  Cenbank seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 1998\par 17:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Oct 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  or interbank market Thursday after the peso tumbled to a new historic low in early trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars through private banks after the peso tumbled 10.11 pesos against the dollar to 1,579. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed the drop to speculation about a possible devaluation in Brazil following Sunday's presidential elections, and to Wednesday's warning from Moody's Investors Service about a possible downgrade of key Colombian ratings. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were unavailable for immediate comment on the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the peso closed sharply lower Wednesday, after giving up 13.25 pesos against the dollar to end at 1,563.05. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported an active 137 trades in the first hour of Thursday's trading for a total of just over $100 million. \par \par \uc2  (( - Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua10157x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
