\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  cenbank admits  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1998\par 01:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Sept 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that it had sold about $130 million on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  or interbank market in the aftermath of Wednesday's de facto devaluation of the peso. \par \par \uc2  Roberto Junguito, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board of directors, said the market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were designed to "cool off uncertainty and speculation" after the bank raised the peso's exchange rate band by nine percentage points, allowing for a faster daily depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Junguito, who spoke to reporters on the sidelines of an economic seminar in the capital, said the bank's dollar sales included $80 million Wednesday, when the peso plunged 82.68 pesos on the dollar to close at 1,526.00. \par \par \uc2  It sold an additional $50 million from its international reserves Thursday, when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended 6.8 pesos lower against the dollar at 1,532.8, Junguito said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar sales, aimed at lending the peso much-needed albeit artificial support, were significant since turnover on the thinly-traded interbank market totalled just $528.2 million over the two days. \par \par \uc2  The bank's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market brought the total amount of dollars it sold from its reserves, now thought to total less than $9 billion, to $347.65 million since last Friday \par \par \uc2 