\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  peso ends lower, c-bank said to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 21:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Sept 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso ended 6.8 pesos lower against the dollar Thursday, closing at 1,532.8 in a market that traders said had seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at lending support to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market was calmer, but there's still demand (for dollars) from the corporate sector," one trader said in a phone interview. \par \par \uc2  He said there was nothing like the turmoil that buffeted the market Wednesday, when the peso nosedived by 82.68 against the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to change its exchange rate band and allow for a de facto devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But several traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling dollars, for at least the sixth consecutive session, in a bid to bolster the peso and satisfy continuing demand for greenbacks from foreign funds liquidating local assets. \par \par \uc2  "The bank continued selling, in fact it was even more than it might have sold before the devaluation," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials could not be reached to confirm the dollar sales or comment on how much cash had been drawn from the bank's foreign reserves since last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported 326 trades fo a total of $258.2 million and said the peso sank to an intraday low of 1,537.50 before firming ahead of the close. \par \par \uc2  (( - Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944, fax 571 610 7733, bogota.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9300qg8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
