\par\par \b \uc2  Colombian Peso Closes Weaker; Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 22:33\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--Two days after \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised eyebrows across Latin America with an unexpected devaluation, the peso continued losing ground against the dollar Thursday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The weakening came even as the bank sold millions of dollars as a support mechanism, they added. \par \par \uc2  The peso's average exchange rate rose to 1531.82 to the dollar from 1523.48 Wednesday, marking a depreciation. However, the peso's drop was small compared with a 5% depreciation seen the previous day, just hours after the bank announced it was shifting its preset trading band nine percentage points higher. \par \par \uc2  "The bank has lost a lot of credibility, and now they still have to sell the same reserves (to defend the peso)," said one trader who was disappointed with the bank's decision. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the peso might hit the ceiling of the new band in coming weeks he said, "For me there is no ceiling. They demonstrated to me that the band can be broken." \par \par \uc2  Bank board members summoned to speak before a congressional committee Thursday said the de facto devaluation had passed by a 4-3 vote, and co-director Salomon Kalmanovitz said he was one of those voting against the measure. \par \par \uc2  The decision came on the back of three consecutive days in which the peso's exchange rate stuck to the weak side of the band, prompting the bank to sell some $200 million as a support mechanism. \par \par \uc2  However, traders said the bank had to sell another $100 million on Wednesday to prevent the peso from surging towards the weak side of the new band, and some estimated the bank sold at least that amount again on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume came in at $270 million, slightly above normal levels, as banks and private companies stocked up on dollars to protect themselves from any further volatility in the future. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen about 18% against the dollar so far this year.\par -By Ruth Morris; 571-215-7132; rmorris@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  03-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2033GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1068 1845 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du930083y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
